817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,49,1663,551,279,46912,315,57960,37018,90,17,15170,59,26888,58,18,15370,19,92,41715,26888,58,18,15370,18,17,3417,12947,576,4226,646,387,5326,304,279,1352,315,57960,37018,35702,26888,58,18,15370,32,3417,90,33,31716,11,1380,400,32,3,323,400,33,3,525,6785,25780,13,7379,279,8028,3204,897,315,400,32,79726,12947,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nRationalize the denominator of $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4}+\\sqrt[3]{32}}$. The answer can be written in the form of $\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{A}}{B}$, where $A$ and $B$ are positive integers. Find the minimum possible value of $A+B$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f4cf47652a172a1cb43ba23bd0aaf9016e63a813ab040c23f0e15feeb86901ac"},"seconds":7.981455564498901,"seed":198454375233219430,"stop":"eos","text":"To rationalize the denominator of \\(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4}+\\sqrt[3]{32}}\\), we start by recognizing that \\(\\sqrt[3]{32} = \\sqrt[3]{2^5} = 2\\sqrt[3]{4}\\). Therefore, the expression can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2\\sqrt[3]{4}} = \\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{4}}\n\\]\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt[3]{16}\\) (which is \\((\\sqrt[3]{4})^2\\)):\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{4}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{16}}{\\sqrt[3]{16}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt[3]{16}}{3 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{2\\sqrt[3]{16}}{12} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{16}}{6}\n\\]\nThis expression is in the form \\(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{A}}{B}\\) where \\(A = 16\\) and \\(B = 6\\). Therefore, the minimum possible value of \\(A + B\\) is:\n\\[\n16 + 6 = 22\n\\]\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{22}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{22}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:662"}
